// Windows resource script: gives mirobody_qt.exe its Explorer / Start-menu / taskbar
// icon. Windows reads that from a resource compiled INTO the binary, so a loose .ico
// beside the exe would do nothing -- this file is the only way to attach it.
//
// The first ICON in the resource table is the one the shell uses for the file itself,
// which is why the id is the conventional lowest one. Both resource compilers this
// repo builds with (MSVC rc.exe and mingw windres) resolve the path relative to this
// .rc file, so the bare filename is correct for both.
//
// mirobody.ico is generated -- see gen_icon.py.
IDI_ICON1 ICON "mirobody.ico"
